{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he was in Keziv when she bore him.</b> What does Scripture come to inform us — that Judah was in a certain place when she bore him? Rashi explains: because her bearing ceased, the place was called Keziv. And the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote that she called him Shelah from the root שגגה, after the name of the place, for he was in Keziv when she bore him; and the inadvertent (שוגג) is false (כוזב) in his thought." "<b>And it is possible</b> to say that there is a hidden matter in this verse, and the word כזיב is a number that interchanges in the great and unique Name (כוזו), and it is good for prayer, since you already know that it is investigated from the third — there being the place of the sons — as is known from the commandment of sending the mother bird and from the prayer of Hannah. And Scripture reveals to you in this that after she bore Shelah, who is the third, Judah was praying in the power of that Name when she bore him, that He would give him worthy sons, the seed of men, in the manner of what is said (1 Samuel 1:11) regarding Hannah: ״ונתת לאמתך זרע אנשים״, for he knew by the holy spirit that the essence of his seed was not from those three. And behold the matter rolled about in Tamar his daughter-in-law, and she bore him twins — and this is what our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: ״ותהר לו״ — a righteous one like him, a mighty one like him. And behold the word בכזיב equals בכח כוזו זכה יהודה בתאומים ('By the power of כוזו Judah merited twins')."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:35.348582184Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}